From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 10:45:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] network: Editor pages on the window's navigation, IPv4/IPv6
 fit a phone

Plinius: as a page of the window's navigation the editor still had a
navigation of its own inside, and the back swipe did not get through
it: neither on "Add VPN" nor on the settings pages. The editor now
takes its own navigation apart when it is a page: the first page's
content goes straight into the page, the settings pages (and the
settings of a picked VPN type) go on the window's navigation. The
header bars show the window's back arrow, which replaces the arrow made
from Cancel, and the swipe works everywhere.

IPv4 and IPv6 were wider than the screen and scrolled sideways, which
also swallowed the swipe: the methods now stand one below the other
under the heading, address and route entries are narrower (they still
grow on a wider page), margins as on the other pages.
---
